    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5050" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμβλυ-ώσσω</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμβλύ-ττω</span></b> , only in
		pres.: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμβλύς</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be short-sighted, have weak
				sight,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Prorrh.</u>
				2.42
			</span></i>, etc., <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				508c
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hp.Mi.</u>
				374d
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πρὸς τὸ φῶς</span>
			<i>to be dazzled</i> by it, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Cont.</u>
				1
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				5.163a
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τὰ τηλικαῦτα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Tim.</u>
					27
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ τοῦ γήρως ἀμβλυῶττον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.13e
				</span></i>
			.</div>
